  {
   "title": "Rules in one line each",
   "kind": "list",
   "items": [
    "Cation first, anion second, always.",
    "Ionic (Types I, II, IV): NO prefixes. Covalent (Type III): prefixes, never mono- first.",
    "Roman numeral = the metal's charge, not a count. Zn, Ag, Cd never; Pb, Sn always.",
    "Find the charge: total negative charge ÷ number of metal atoms.",
    "Polyatomic ions never change; use parentheses for more than one.",
    "Ionic formulas reduce (CaO); covalent formulas don't (N₂O₄).",
    "Acids: no O → hydro-…-ic; -ate → -ic; -ite → -ous; keep per- and hypo-.",
    "Hydrates: name + prefix + hydrate (CuSO₄·5H₂O copper(II) sulfate pentahydrate).",
    "Anion charge = group number − 8 (S in 6A → 2−). H₂O = water, NH₃ = ammonia."
